From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:38:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] board: mediatek-mobile: restart the watchdog right
 before the OS jump

The DRAM-wide cache flush before an OS boot takes about 8 s of the 15 s
watchdog timeout. Restart the watchdog in the last C hook before the jump
so the OS has the full timeout to reach its watchdog driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
index 498c8d73467..1b637e882c1 100644
--- a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
@@ -594,6 +594,18 @@ void board_cleanup_before_linux(void)
 	gd->ram_size = end - start;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Last C hook before the jump to the OS (after the cache flush above, which
+ * takes seconds): restart the running RGU watchdog so the OS gets its full
+ * timeout to reach its own watchdog driver.
+ */
+void update_os_arch_secondary_cores(uint8_t os_arch)
+{
+	if (CONFIG_MEDIATEK_MOBILE_ENTRY_WDT_RESTART)
+		writel(CONFIG_MEDIATEK_MOBILE_ENTRY_WDT_RESTART_KEY,
+		       (void *)CONFIG_MEDIATEK_MOBILE_ENTRY_WDT_RESTART);
+}
+
 int dram_init(void)
 {
 	if (mtk_select_window()) {
